WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.369 --> 00:00:16.150
The pirates' ship was indeed very interesting.

2
00:00:16.970 --> 00:00:19.611
In every room, the animals found something new.

3
00:00:19.631 --> 00:00:21.192
"Look at this bed!"

4
00:00:21.712 --> 00:00:22.933
Gub-Gub jumped on it.

5
00:00:22.953 --> 00:00:25.153
"The pillows and blanket are silk!"

6
00:00:27.194 --> 00:00:28.855
Dab-Dab opened the closet.

7
00:00:29.735 --> 00:00:31.096
He tried on the slippers.

8
00:00:31.836 --> 00:00:32.776
They wouldn't fit.

9
00:00:32.796 --> 00:00:35.258
"WOW! Look at this!"

10
00:00:36.218 --> 00:00:38.639
Dab-Dab pulled out a large pirate's hat.

11
00:00:39.599 --> 00:00:42.300
"I am the Great Barbary DUCK!"

12
00:00:43.321 --> 00:00:45.122
Dab-Dab said in a low voice.

13
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:48.923
There was so much to see.

14
00:00:49.463 --> 00:00:52.645
In one room, they found gold, silver, and jewels.

15
00:00:53.465 --> 00:00:54.966
It was the pirates' treasure.

16
00:00:54.986 --> 00:01:01.508
"Dr. Dolittle won't have to worry about money anymore," said Gub-Gub.

17
00:01:01.568 --> 00:01:02.328
"Don't touch it!"

18
00:01:02.789 --> 00:01:03.489
snapped Jip.

19
00:01:03.509 --> 00:01:06.170
"The pirates stole this from people."

20
00:01:06.190 --> 00:01:10.312
"We can't return it," Gub-Gub rubbed his hand.

21
00:01:10.332 --> 00:01:12.273
"But it's not ours!"

22
00:01:12.673 --> 00:01:13.373
growled Jip.

23
00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:14.613
"Don't touch it!"

24
00:01:16.474 --> 00:01:18.935
Dab-Dab found a door he couldn't open.

25
00:01:18.955 --> 00:01:22.537
"I wonder what's behind this door?"

26
00:01:23.197 --> 00:01:23.737
he asked.

27
00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:26.698
The others came over and tried to open it.

28
00:01:26.718 --> 00:01:30.320
"Maybe it's more treasures," guessed Gub-Gub.

29
00:01:31.108 --> 00:01:32.729
Dab-Dab's eyes got big.

30
00:01:32.749 --> 00:01:38.372
"Maybe maybe the pirates put bodies in there."

31
00:01:41.754 --> 00:01:44.396
Dr. Dolittle was enjoying a quiet moment.

32
00:01:45.176 --> 00:01:46.937
He was thinking about the monkeys.

33
00:01:47.738 --> 00:01:50.479
He was thinking about Polynesia and Chee-Chee.

34
00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:53.361
And he was thinking about Puddleby.

35
00:01:53.381 --> 00:01:55.402
"DR. DOLITTLE!"

36
00:01:56.442 --> 00:01:58.804
All the animals started talking at once.

37
00:01:59.924 --> 00:02:00.985
"Slow down!

38
00:02:01.185 --> 00:02:04.708
I can't understand any of you," the doctor said.

39
00:02:05.509 --> 00:02:06.590
Jip spoke first.

40
00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.373
"We found a room, but the door is locked."

41
00:02:11.133 --> 00:02:16.017
"We think," gulped Dab-Dab, "there are bodies inside."

42
00:02:16.398 --> 00:02:19.000
"Bodies?" the doctor said, alarmed.

43
00:02:21.282 --> 00:02:24.304
Dr. Dolittle followed the animals to the locked room.

44
00:02:24.324 --> 00:02:25.745
"Oh, my!

45
00:02:26.185 --> 00:02:27.727
Look at all this gold!"

46
00:02:28.287 --> 00:02:28.988
he remarked.

47
00:02:29.612 --> 00:02:30.913
"Over here, Doctor!"

48
00:02:31.753 --> 00:02:33.334
Dab-Dab pointed to the door.

49
00:02:33.354 --> 00:02:37.676
"Well, let's see if we can find the key," said the doctor.

50
00:02:38.437 --> 00:02:40.358
Everyone started to look for a key.

51
00:02:42.119 --> 00:02:47.162
While they were looking, Too-Too suddenly said: "There's someone inside."

52
00:02:47.962 --> 00:02:49.363
Everyone became silent.

53
00:02:49.383 --> 00:02:53.345
"I don't hear anything, Too-Too," said the doctor.

54
00:02:54.005 --> 00:02:55.466
But Too-Too was listening.

55
00:02:55.486 --> 00:02:58.328
"There it is again!

56
00:02:59.104 --> 00:03:00.024
Don't you hear that?"

57
00:03:01.005 --> 00:03:02.626
But nobody could hear a thing.

58
00:03:03.726 --> 00:03:05.807
Too-Too leaned closer against the door.

59
00:03:05.827 --> 00:03:07.928
"What do you hear?"

60
00:03:08.548 --> 00:03:09.149
asked Jip.

61
00:03:10.489 --> 00:03:14.551
"Someone is putting their hands in their pockets," replied the owl.

62
00:03:15.211 --> 00:03:17.552
The others looked at each other and smiled.

63
00:03:18.513 --> 00:03:19.713
"How can you hear that?

64
00:03:20.394 --> 00:03:26.940
That doesn't make any sound at all," giggled Dab-Dab.

65
00:03:26.980 --> 00:03:28.982
Too-Too gave Dab-Dab a long stare.

66
00:03:29.002 --> 00:03:31.964
"We owls have very good ears.

67
00:03:32.504 --> 00:03:36.827
Besides, everything makes a sound," Too-Too explained.

68
00:03:36.847 --> 00:03:39.969
"How interesting," said the doctor.

69
00:03:39.989 --> 00:03:42.111
"What's he doing now?"

70
00:03:42.131 --> 00:03:45.933
"He's rubbing his face," Too-Too reported.

71
00:03:45.953 --> 00:03:47.474
"It's a woman.

72
00:03:48.135 --> 00:03:49.596
NO! It's a man."

73
00:03:52.017 --> 00:03:53.318
Dab-Dab was right.

74
00:03:53.778 --> 00:03:55.800
There was a body inside the room.

75
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:57.961
Except it wasn't dead.

76
00:03:58.762 --> 00:03:59.922
It was still alive.

77
00:04:00.923 --> 00:04:03.325
Too-Too looked through the lock for a long time.

78
00:04:03.345 --> 00:04:06.547
"The man inside is very sad.

79
00:04:07.227 --> 00:04:09.849
He is crying," he said finally.

80
00:04:09.869 --> 00:04:12.370
"Then let's help him get out!"

81
00:04:13.111 --> 00:04:13.911
said the doctor.
